    {
      "env": {
        "SCALA_WORKSPACE_ROOT": "/tmp"
      },
      "args": [
        "workspace_file",
        {
          "op": "write",
          "path": "../escape.txt",
          "content": "x"
        }
      ],
      "note": "The refusal is LEXICAL, so it fires whatever the root is — which is why this is a plain call and not a step in the round trip. A write that escaped would land outside the workspace with the operator's own privileges; the message names the path and the rule so a caller can see which one it broke.",
      "expect": {
        "ok": false,
        "error": "write refused: '../escape.txt' resolves outside the workspace root"
      },
      "export": "executeCodingLocally",
      "module": "src/executors/coding-local.ts",
      "package": "@teamscala/tool-executor",
      "suite_type": "function_call",
      "slug": "tool-executor:a-write-outside-the-workspace-is-refused"
    },
    {
      "env": {
        "SCALA_WORKSPACE_ROOT": "/proc/1/root-not-writable"
      },
      "args": [
        "workspace_file",
        {
          "op": "read",
          "path": "x"
        }
      ],
      "note": "NO ROUTING ELSEWHERE. A root the process cannot write is a refusal, not a fallback to the cwd or the repo — silently operating somewhere other than where the operator pointed is how a coding op edits a file nobody named. expect_error because the read refuses rather than answering.",
      "expect": {
        "ok": false,
        "error": "workspace_file refused: this process cannot write /proc/1/root-not-writable; the coding layer runs only in the engine of the lane that holds the repositories, never from another lane or a cloud caller"
      },
      "export": "executeCodingLocally",
      "module": "src/executors/coding-local.ts",
      "package": "@teamscala/tool-executor",
      "suite_type": "function_call",
      "slug": "tool-executor:an-unowned-workspace-refuses-rather-than-routing-elsewhere"
